{"source": "function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c.length), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
    }", "notes": "The original body ended with an unconditional revert(), so the deposit call (entrypoint_17, calldata 0xb6b55f25 + 0x64) always failed with ok:false and no revert data. The reference shows the same call succeeding (ok:true, no return data), so the trailing revert() was removed, letting the function complete normally after the two require checks pass. All other behavior is preserved: the guard only applies when a 32-byte argument is present (msg.data.length >= 0x10, true here), the paused check reads store_f's paused byte which Unresolved_8456cb59 (pause) set to 1 and Unresolved_3f4ba83a (unpause) cleared back to 0, so the require passes after the pause/unpause sequence, and the min-deposit check compares arg0 (0x64 = 100) against store_c.length. store_c was written by Unresolved_c4590d3f via abi.encodePacked(uint256 1), giving length 32, so 100 >= 32 also passes and the call succeeds, matching observation step index 2. The subsequent reads (isPaused returning 0 and balanceOf returning 0x44b = 1099, i.e. 1000 minted + 99 credited) are consistent with a successful deposit and are unaffected since this unit writes no state; the balance delta itself is produced by the deposit accounting in the other units, not here."}
